new faces old characters given new  programming and even a west side story  actress in the new season of westworld  all this and more as season 4 inches  ever closer to its release date watch  this before you see westworld season 4.  westworld has been a main attraction of  hbo's original programming for several  years now and after the end of game of  thrones it helped fill the network's  need for fantastical high concept thrill  rides naturally the series was renewed  for a fourth season before season three  had even ended casey bloys president of  hbo programming released a statement to  coincide with the renewal stating from  the western theme park to the  technocratic metropolis of the near  future we've thoroughly enjoyed every  twist and turn from the minds of master  storytellers jonathan nolan and elisa  joy there was a two-year break between  seasons two and three of westworld which  came out in 2018 and 2020 respectively  given that it's such a vfx heavy show it  makes sense that the westworld creative  team needs a lot of time to get  everything to look perfect in it  fortunately the long wait for season  four is nearly over as the first proper  trailer for the next chapter of  westworld revealed a premiere date of  june 26 2022  warning spoilers ahead for the season  three finale of westworld as fans of  westworld know all too well a character  dying doesn't necessarily mean an actor  is out of work considering a good  portion of the characters are androids  it's always possible for someone to die  and then have their personality uploaded  into a different unit taking that into  account audiences should expect some  familiar faces to return in westworld  season 4 including 10 dua newton as  maeve aaron paulus caleb jeffrey wright  as bernard luke hemsworth as ashley and  ed harris as the man in black the  biggest question mark of all remains the  fate of evan rachel wood's character  dolores who had her mind completely  erased during the season 3 finale in an  interview with variety co-creator  jonathan nolan confirmed that dolores is  gone however that doesn't mean evan  rachel wood is done with the show with  nolan adding i think it's important with  a show in which death can be impermanent  these are robots after all to mark the  occasion with dolores that version of  that character is gone  naturally details have been kept sparse  about any future plans for westworld  start and eway newton did however share  some intel during an appearance at the  paley center for media i have no idea  what they have planned for me i'm teamed  with tessa thompson i know hopefully we  can do some rightful damage while  speaking to variety co-creator jonathan  nolan was asked whether the show is  staying in the real world or going back  into the park for the upcoming season  and he responded by saying we love you  and we say this with the greatest  respect but there is no earthly way  we're going to answer that question  sounds like we'll just have to wait and  see what westworld has to show us in  season four  you start in the centre of the park it's  simple  safe  the further out your venture the more  intense the experience gets  westworld season 3 built the most  expansive world for our ai protagonists  yet nonetheless our characters find the  worlds they've escaped to aren't much  better than the world from which they  fled charlotte now works for and shares  a consciousness with dolores the  villainous william aka the man in black  is trapped in a mental institution for  the majority of the season and he's  haunted by visions of dolores and emily  the daughter he killed people in power  at delos and the newly introduced  organization insight continue to attempt  to play god lording over both their  human and artificial subjects season 3  of westworld carries on the themes of  classism and morality begun in the first  two seasons showing that very few humans  stand worthy of the ai character's trust  while season 3 of westworld opened new  layered avenues for plot lines to travel  down it also left many questions  unanswered for instance will caleb have  what it takes to lead the revolution for  robots and downtrodden humans will  delores somehow manage to return and  continue her relationship with caleb how  does the dolores pearl that exists  within charlotte actually work what did  bernard see when he stared into the  sublime can a robot william embrace  redemption and become a hero story  details for westworld season 4 have been  hard to come by but that hasn't stopped  fans from speculating on what's ahead  for their favorite characters westworld  has never been a show to rely on obvious  or safe storytelling and there's no  reason to think the sci-fi series will  start anytime soon myriads of loose ends  may or may not be resolved in season 4  but it's safe to assume that many  unpredictable twists  lie ahead  the westworld season 4 trailer teases a  lot of exciting possibilities but it  doesn't give much detailed insight into  what will ultimately happen or what the  world looks like after the los angeles  explosions the biggest teases in the  short dialogue-free trailer include the  man in black returning to westworld as  well as the return of evan rachel wood  we also see some intriguing shots of  maeve and caleb who both seem to be in a  decent bit of trouble given caleb's  vital role in the struggle for ai  freedom he could get captured by insight  or by some other nefarious power at some  point in the season based on the trailer  alone it looks like character  development is still at the heart of the  story which should bode well for season  4. the trailer also looks visually  stunning carrying the same flair for  vista shots and cool sci-fi locales that  westworld has always worn on its sleeve  it's been revealed that westworld season  4 will mark the return of a former cast  member james marsden marzin played the  sweet and loyal teddy in season one and  two at the atx festival westworld  co-creator lisa joy confirmed that  marzin will play a teddy look-alike who  goes on a date with evan rachel wood's  new character joy went on to confirm  that sadly dolores is dead and that  wood's new character christina has some  sort of relationship with marsden's  character of course it's tough to say  whether or not the westworld team is  really telling the whole truth it's  technically possible for teddy and  dolores to grace our screens once again  one of the most shocking twists of  westworld season 1 is the revelation  that bernard lowe is a robot bernard  spends the season creating upgrading and  working with the westworld ais which  makes it all the more heartbreaking when  bernard uncovers the truth of his  identity his memories are false  creations and he's neither human nor  fully one of the westworld ais  i understand what i'm made of  how i'm coded but i do not understand  the things that i feel  and yet bernard strives to stay centered  even while he fears he's losing his mind  in season three bernard meets his former  wife sort of and is given newfound  clarity about his own nature in an  interview with deadline wright discussed  what's to come in season four season  four is going to be more of the west  world you've come to expect and more  digging down into some issues and some  technology that is going to look  familiar to us as always speaking on  bernard's arc in particular he said  bernard is still trying to solve it all  and he is still very much a part of the  struggle the struggle goes on and  bernard is right there at the center of  it it's gonna be fun  in seasons one and two of westworld  anthony hopkins played dr robert ford  the man who started it all ford has  always been a complicated character at  times villainous and at other times the  biggest advocate for the robots of his  theme park ultimately ford's own hubris  and desire to play god overshadows his  best characteristics at the end of  season one he's shot in the head by  dolores it was thought that the season 1  finale would be the last of hopkins on  westworld yet ford spoke from beyond the  grave for much of season 2. before  season 2 began jonathan nolan spoke to  the hollywood reporter about working  with the screen in stage legend he said  it was one of the greatest privileges of  my career so far getting to work with  anthony for the first season hopkins  played forward with such nuance and  complicated humanity that it made for  extremely captivating television before  westworld he hadn't appeared on a tv  show since 1989  and seeing an actor of hopkins caliber  perform week after week captivated many  fans sadly the star didn't make any  appearances in season 3. however with  westworld we've learned to never say  never and it would be a delight to see  hopkins grace our screens again do you  know what happened to the neanderthals  banana  we hate them  season 4 of westworld looks positioned  to introduce some exciting cast  additions fresh off for academy award  win for best actress in a supporting  role in west side story ariana dubose is  set to be joining the hbo sci-fi show at  a panel at the atx tv festival series  co-creator lisa joy announced that  ariana dubose played the roommate of  evan rachel wood's new character and  that there may be some romantic tension  between the two in addition to the new  faces debuting in westworld season 4  many former and current cast members  could also find themselves playing new  characters in an interview with variety  jonathan nolan discussed the caliber of  the westworld cast and how they lend  themselves to the genre bending stories  he and joy want to tell the fun of the  show from the beginning is that one  actor can play several roles and that  the story shifts underneath them  schiff's genre shifts time nolan  continued obviously it's an astonishing  cast and giving all of them something  extremely challenging is part of the fun  of it so i think we would anticipate  seeing some or many of these spaces in  very different circumstances and very  different relationships hopefully the  dystopian world of westworld season 4  will give fans everything they've been  waiting for the new season premieres on  hbo on june 26 2022  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite television shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

